  "synthesis": {
    "description": "A round starts when someone in contracts or logistics finds contracts that need to end, or when a counterparty wants out. The requester asks a contract administrator to prepare and send a termination letter, sometimes with a next-day deadline, and other contracts awaiting termination get added to the same request. Counterparties terminating on their side are told to send a letter of termination by fax.",
    "steps": [
      "Identify the contract or contracts that need to be terminated.",
      "Check the contract terms for whether and how it can be terminated and what notice applies.",
      "Ask contract administration to prepare and send the termination letter by a stated date.",
      "Prepare the letter and send it to the counterparty, or receive the counterparty's faxed letter.",
      "Update the contract record to show the termination."
    ],
    "approach": "A standard termination letter with fields for contract number, counterparty, effective date and notice clause, plus a short intake checklist that confirms the termination terms before the letter goes out and records the date it was sent or received.",
    "rationale": "The quotes show repeated requests to prepare and send the same kind of letter, often several contracts at once and against a short deadline. A ready letter with the variable fields marked removes most of the drafting, while the terms check stays with the contract administrator.",
    "artifact_type": "email_template"
  },
